-- 20050  artemia-50-soft-granulate  (artemia-soft-150g)
UPDATE public.products SET
  image_url = 'https://vumjslsogdnexehutibj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/products/discusfood/artemia-soft-150g.jpg',
  description = E'The softening prevents the granules from swelling in the aquarium water or in the digestive tract of the fish and at the same time increases the acceptance of the food. The grain size of approx. 1mm qualifies the soft granulate primarily for small to medium ornamental fish species.\n\nArtemia 50% Softgranulate XL, approx. 1.5 – 2 mm, is suitable for medium to large fish.\n\nExperience has shown that Artemia 50% Softgranulat is not only well received by ornamental fish, many shrimp lovers have also discovered this high-yield complete food for themselves or their charges.',
  details = E'Ingredients: artemia 50%, plant proteins, rice flour, salmon oil, garlic 4%, brewer''s yeast, kelp, amino acids, minerals, prebiotics and probiotics.\nAnalytical components: Crude protein 49.3%, crude fat 7%, crude ash 2.4%, crude fiber 0.7%.\nAdditives per kg: Vitamins: A (3a672a) 20000 IU, C (3a300) 150 mg, D3 (3a671) 1500 IU; with colorants; trace elements: Fe (E 1) 24 mg, Mn (3b502) 31 mg, Zn (3b603) 30 mg; with antioxidants.\nFeeding recommendation: feed 2-3 times daily as much as the fish will eat within 2-5 minutes. Do not overfeed the fish!\nStorage: Not for human consumption! Store in a cool, dry place!\nProduct Nr.: 20050',
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'artemia-50-soft-granulate';

-- 20051  artemia-50-flat-granulate  (artemia-flat-65g)
UPDATE public.products SET
  image_url = 'https://vumjslsogdnexehutibj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/products/discusfood/artemia-flat-65g.jpg',
  description = E'"Don`t call it flake!"\n\n..., because this is a flat granulate in the form of a flake. Extrusion enables the production of the highest possible germ-free product. All pressure- and heat-sensitive components are added only after this manufacturing step, so that they are preserved in their structure and thus remain completely effective. The stable and relatively large shape of the individual, flake-like granules and the special sinking behavior favors rapid acceptance. Even delicate wild-caught discus begin to eat the flat granules greedily after a short acclimation, thanks to the high food quality and the special sinking and swimming behavior Artemia 50%.\n\nOf course, there is nothing to be said against offering the granules somewhat crushed to all other types of aquarium fish, regardless of size. Another advantage of the relatively long surface residence time is that even very timid and shy surface feeders can be catered for. This can, for example, facilitate the feeding of new stock.\n\nThe pure artemia content of 50% is an argument in its own right compared to other conventional feeds. In combination with valuable plant proteins, vitamins, minerals and high-quality fatty acids, a complete staple food is created, suitable for almost all freshwater and saltwater fish. Please always follow the feeding recommendation as it can be found on each can.',
  details = E'Ingredients: artemia 50%, vegetable proteins, rice flour, salmon oil, garlic 4%, brewer''s yeast, kelp, amino acids, minerals, prebiotics and probiotics.\nAnalytical components: Crude protein 49.3%, crude fat 7%, crude ash 2.4%, crude fiber 0.7%.\nAdditives per kg: Vitamins: A (3a672a) 20000 IU, C (3a300) 150 mg, D3 (3a671) 1500 IU; with colorants; trace elements: Fe (E 1) 24 mg, Mn (3b502) 31 mg, Zn (3b603) 30 mg; with antioxidants.\nFeeding recommendation: feed 2-3 times daily as much as the fish will eat within 2-5 minutes. Do not overfeed the fish!\nStorage: Not for human consumption! Store in a cool, dry place!\nProduct Nr.: 20051',
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'artemia-50-flat-granulate';

