-- 20057  herbs-food  (herbs-food)
UPDATE public.products SET
  image_url = 'https://vumjslsogdnexehutibj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/products/discusfood/herbs-food.png',
  description = E'Discusfood Herbs Food – Natural herbal feed for healthy freshwater ornamental fish Support for gut health, the immune system and recovery Discusfood Herbs Food is a high-quality functional feed for all freshwater ornamental fish. The balanced formula has been specially developed to provide optimal support for fish during stressful situations such as transport, relocation, quarantine, introduction to a new tank or following periods of stress.\n\nThe combination of valuable medicinal herbs, herbal oils, spirulina, chlorella and modern probiotics and prebiotics promotes a stable gut flora and supports the natural regeneration of the digestive system. A healthy gut is the foundation for efficient nutrient absorption, a strong immune system and healthy, resilient fish.\n\nNatural power from medicinal herbs The carefully selected medicinal herbs and herbal oils provide numerous phytochemicals that have been valued for centuries for their beneficial properties. They can help to stabilise digestion, support metabolism and promote the fish’s general well-being.\n\nA balanced diet is crucial, particularly after transport stress or during a quarantine period, to relieve strain on the organism and strengthen its natural defences.\n\nWith spirulina and chlorella – the power of microalgae A key component of Discusfood Herbs Food is its high content of spirulina and chlorella.\n\nSpirulina is one of the most valuable microalgae in modern aquaculture. It contains high-quality protein, natural carotenoids, vitamins, minerals and antioxidant plant compounds. Scientific studies show that spirulina can have a positive effect on the growth, vitality and natural immune defences of fish. Furthermore, spirulina supports the development of intense and natural colours.\n\nChlorella complements this effect through its high content of chlorophyll, amino acids, vitamins and bioactive plant compounds. Both microalgae provide high-quality plant-based protein and are considered a particularly valuable addition to the diet of ornamental fish.\n\nProbiotics and prebiotics – For healthy gut flora A stable gut flora plays a central role in fish health, feed utilisation and resilience.\n\nProbiotics are beneficial microorganisms that can support the natural balance in the digestive tract.\n\nPrebiotics serve as food for these beneficial bacteria and promote their proliferation.\n\nThe combination of probiotics and prebiotics – also known as a synbiotic – is specifically used in modern aquaculture to support the gut health, immune function and stress resistance of fish. Studies show positive effects on digestion, growth and the general health of ornamental and farmed fish.\n\nHigh-quality protein sources for optimal nutrition The formula is based on easily digestible and biologically high-quality raw materials:\n\nInsect protein Krill Shrimp meal Squid meal Spirulina Chlorella Medicinal herb mix Herbal oils Salmon oil Probiotics Prebiotics\n\nThis balanced combination provides essential amino acids, valuable omega-3 fatty acids, natural vitamins and important trace elements for a species-appropriate diet.\n\nThe benefits at a glance ✓ Supports gut health and digestion\n\n✓ Ideal after transport, stress and quarantine\n\n✓ Contains valuable medicinal herbs and herbal oils\n\n✓ Contains spirulina and chlorella\n\n✓ With probiotics and prebiotics to support gut flora\n\n✓ Promotes vitality and resilience\n\n✓ High-quality animal and plant-based protein sources\n\n✓ Suitable for all freshwater ornamental fish\n\nDiscusfood Herbs Food – where healthy nutrition and natural support go hand in hand.',
  details = E'Ingredients: Insect protein, rice, medicinal herb mix, squid meal, krill, rye, oats, shrimp meal, peas, brewer''s yeast, dried algae spirulina, chlorella, salmon oil, herbal oils, prebiotics, probiotics.\nAnalytical components: Protein 38%, fat content 6.7%, inorganic matter 7%, crude fibre 4.3%.\nAdditives per kg: Vitamins: A (3a672a) 28000 IU, C (3a300) 210 mg, D3 (3a671) 2100 IU; Trace elements: Fe (3b103) 34 mg, Mn (3b502) 43 mg, Zn (3b603) 42 mg; with antioxidants.\nFeeding recommendation: Feed 1-2 times daily in quantities that the fish can consume within approx. 30 minutes.\nStorage: Not for human consumption! Store in a cool, dry place!\nProduct Nr.: 20057',
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'herbs-food';

