-- 31000  bacto-bakterien  (bacto)
UPDATE public.products SET
  image_url = 'https://vumjslsogdnexehutibj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/products/discusfood/bacto.webp',
  description = E'Liquid filter starter for a safe start to your aquarium Discusfood Bacto+ with Zeolite supports the rapid establishment of stable biological filter performance and lays the foundation for permanently healthy aquarium water. The live nitrifying bacteria it contains colonise filter media and surfaces, where they reliably convert ammonium and nitrite into the significantly less harmful nitrate.\n\nThe innovative combination of highly concentrated bacterial cultures and high-quality zeolite offers a decisive advantage: zeolite binds ammonium whilst simultaneously providing an ideal colonisation surface for beneficial filter bacteria. This accelerates the development of biological filter performance and reduces the risk of critical ammonia and nitrite spikes, particularly during the running-in phase or after filter cleaning.\n\nIdeally suited for:\n\nSetting up new aquariums Water changes and filter cleaning Introducing new fish Support following medication treatments Freshwater aquariums of all sizes\n\nYour benefits at a glance:\n\nRapid development of an effective biological filter Supports the natural nitrogen cycle Reduces the risk of ammonium and nitrite build-up Contains high-quality zeolite for additional biological support Suitable for all biological filter systems Promotes consistently stable water parameters and the well-being of your fish\n\nWith Discusfood Bacto+, you can create the ideal conditions for a biologically stable aquarium – right from day one.\n\nSources used Scientific study: Application of zeolite filters in fish breeding recirculation systems and their effect on nitrifying bacteria, Aquaculture (2020). Shows that zeolite binds ammonium, improves water quality and supports the growth of nitrifying bacteria.',
  details = E'Storage: Not for human consumption! Store in a cool, dry place!\nProduct Nr.: 31000',
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'bacto-bakterien';

-- 33020  discus-minerals  (discus-minerals)
UPDATE public.products SET
  image_url = 'https://vumjslsogdnexehutibj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/product-images/products/discusfood/discus-minerals.jpg',
  description = E'Discus Minerals – Minerals and Trace Elements for Discus\n\nPure water (H2O) is a hostile environment. Only dissolved minerals, trace elements and humic substances ensure a healthy environment. Discus Minerals from Discusfood contains a balanced mixture of minerals and trace elements as dissolved in natural waters. Demineralised water (e.g. by osmosis) is used for soft water aquariums. Any natural ingredients are missing. With Discus Minerals the lack of minerals and trace elements can be compensated. The water is mineralised. Discus Minerals is specially optimised for soft water biotopes.\n\nDiscus Minerals counteracts damage caused by mineral deficiency and ensures healthy aquarium water. Discus Minerals does not contain NaCl (table salt) and does not increase the carbonate hardness.',
  details = E'Application: 15 g Discus Minerals to 100 litres of osmosis water or 10 g to 100 litres of mineral-poor water. Discus Minerals is very easily soluble. Dissolve the mineral mixture in a separate container of water and then slowly add to the aquarium. 1 g to 10 litres increases the total hardness by approx. 3∞ GH and the conductivity by approx. 150 µS/cm....\nStorage: Not for human consumption! Store in a cool, dry place!\nProduct Nr.: 33020',
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'discus-minerals';

